{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The son of the hated one he shall acknowledge.</b> For it is a person's way, when he does not wish to do kindness to his relative, to make as though he does not recognize him, as it is written ויתנכר אליה, and it says מדוע מצאתי חן בעיניך להכירני ואנכי נוכריה. Come and learn from this: he must make an acknowledgment of him, or say in the presence of people that he is the firstborn, if he is in a place where they do not know him. And furthermore, come and learn: a person is believed to say, 'This my son is a firstborn.' <b>He shall acknowledge him, to give him.</b> In order to give him — to teach: if a man dies and leaves his wives pregnant, the first to be born has no status of firstborn, for his father did not acknowledge him in his lifetime." "<b>Double portion.</b> Already explained in the portion of Numbers — why a firstborn takes a double portion." "<b>Shall be found to him.</b> To the father, under his hand at the time of death." "<b>For he is the first of his strength.</b> An expression of praise." "<b>To him, the right of the firstborn.</b> And not to a daughter."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:42.371760681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}